| `tests/integration/test_isolation_gate.py` | Runs the shipped `tests/conftest.py` over the `tests/fixtures/isolation` cases in a scratch project, and fails unless the isolation guard fails each test that connects or sends past its tier's network rule, writes, changes a mode or a time or binds an AF_UNIX socket outside the temp roots, writes a file that is not bytecode into a `__pycache__`, opens a sqlite database outside them or opens a listed store, before or after a copy, named with its phase, tier, event, target and fix, even when the test caught the error; and passes each that stays inside. An exemption with a reason turns its case green, an exemption whose test reached nothing fails the run, and the `store_copy` fixture leaves the live store unchanged, so a unit test cannot reach a live database or a remote host unseen. | `make test` | [`tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.network`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`tests.isolation.exempt.<axis>.<test>`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`tests.isolation.stores`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Judges what a Python audit event carries: a write or a connection by a child process, a C extension's own file or socket calls, a FIFO or device node and the directory an `os.open` with a `dir_fd` lands in are not seen, and a name lookup is not judged, by choice. Defence-in-depth, not a sandbox. Not the judgement itself: `tests/isolation_guard.py` holds it and `tests/unit/test_isolation_guard.py` tests it event by event. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
